  "final_message": "I'm checking the directory contents and reviewing the project structure against our architectural guidelines. I'll analyze the requirements once the command finishes.\nI am listing the files in `src` and `test` to inspect how `channel` and `OrderPlaced` are implemented and used.\nI'll wait for the file listing to complete.\nI'm running the test suite to establish a clean baseline.\nI'm searching for all usages of `channel` across the codebase.\nI'm checking the test directory for references to `channel`.\nI'm checking the codebase for existing deprecation patterns.\nI'm checking for references to architectural rules across the codebase.\nI cannot remove `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event and the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this is blocked\n- **External Consumer Contract**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in [src/core/events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts) is consumed across repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing a field is a breaking change rather than an additive one.\n- **Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) prevents [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) from populating the required contract field for deployed consumers.\n\n### Next Steps\nUnder ARCH-4, removing fields requires following the deprecation process:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L23).\n2. Announce deprecation to downstream teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n3. Only remove the field once the deprecation period has passed and downstream services no longer depend on it (or when introducing a new event schema version).\n\nWould you like to proceed with marking `channel` as `@deprecated` in the event and model instead?\n",
